{"urn":"116063","name":"Balksbury Infant School","assessedAt":"2026-08-06","engineVersion":"0.6.0","sourcesScanned":20,"sourceTypes":["school-document","school-website"],"areas":[{"area":"curriculum","score":92,"confidence":0.94,"summary":"Strong publicly visible evidence for curriculum (27 specific items). Listed provision includes mathematics, art, Free Reading Friday, Balksbury Federation Curriculum Model, Balksbury Federation\u2019s Ethos and Culture, ELG: Being Imaginative and Expressive, ELG: Building Relationships, ELG: Fine Motor Skills\u2026.","themes":["curriculum","key stage","mathematics","progress","reading","writing"],"offerings":["mathematics","art","Free Reading Friday","Balksbury Federation Curriculum Model","Balksbury Federation\u2019s Ethos and Culture","ELG: Being Imaginative and Expressive","ELG: Building Relationships","ELG: Fine Motor Skills","ELG: Gross Motor Skills","ELG: Listening, Attention and Understanding","ELG: Managing Self","ELG: Number Patterns","ELG: Past and Present","ELG: People, Culture and Communities","ELG: Self Regulation","ELG: Word Reading","Early Years Framework","Knowledge Engaged Approach","Vision and Values","Encourage Reading Choice"],"signals":[{"text":"supporting reading at home: Pause, Prompt, Praise","sourceUrl":"https://balksburyfederation.co.uk/download/24/curriculum/465/supporting-reading-at-home.pdf","sourceType":"school-document","capturedAt":"2026-08-06","pageTitle":"supporting reading at home","section":"curriculum"},{"text":"balksbury federation curriculum model: Area 5 \u2013 Mathematics","sourceUrl":"https://balksburyfederation.co.uk/download/24/curriculum/466/balksbury-federation-curriculum-model.pdf","sourceType":"school-document","capturedAt":"2026-08-06","pageTitle":"balksbury federation curriculum model","section":"curriculum"},{"text":"balksbury federation curriculum model: through art in positive developmental activities.","sourceUrl":"https://balksburyfederation.co.uk/download/24/curriculum/466/balksbury-federation-curriculum-model.pdf","sourceType":"school-document","capturedAt":"2026-08-06","pageTitle":"balksbury federation curriculum model","section":"curriculum"},{"text":"supporting reading at home: Free Reading Friday","sourceUrl":"https://balksburyfederation.co.uk/download/24/curriculum/465/supporting-reading-at-home.pdf","sourceType":"school-document","capturedAt":"2026-08-06","pageTitle":"supporting reading at home","section":"curriculum"},{"text":"balksbury federation curriculum model: Balksbury Federation Curriculum Model","sourceUrl":"https://balksburyfederation.co.uk/download/24/curriculum/466/balksbury-federation-curriculum-model.pdf","sourceType":"school-document","capturedAt":"2026-08-06","pageTitle":"balksbury federation curriculum model","section":"curriculum"}],"narrativeSummary":"The federation follows the Balksbury Federation Curriculum Model, which includes mathematics as a dedicated area [2]. Reading is supported through home guidance such as Pause, Prompt, Praise, alongside school initiatives including Free Reading Friday [1]. The curriculum also draws on early learning goals covering areas from fine and gross motor skills and number patterns to building relationships and being imaginative and expressive, with subjects such as art included within the federation model and ethos [1][2].","synthesisMethod":"cursor"},{"area":"enrichment","score":40,"confidence":0.25,"summary":"Concrete enrichment and extra-curricular activity details found on the school website. Listed provision includes football, choir, rock choir.","themes":["art","choir","club","enrichment","opportunities","participate"],"offerings":["football","choir","rock choir"],"signals":[{"text":"With 594 free after-school enrichment club places offering a huge range of activities (such as cookery, football, outdoor learning, rock choir and orienteering), children develop social skills alongside those offered by the club.","sourceUrl":"https://balksburyfederation.co.uk/pupil-premium/","sourceType":"school-website","capturedAt":"2026-08-06","pageTitle":"Pupil Premium - Balksbury Federation Infant and Junior Schools","section":"general"}],"narrativeSummary":"The federation offers a substantial after-school enrichment programme, with 594 free club places across a wide range of activities [1]. Listed options include football and rock choir, alongside others such as cookery, outdoor learning and orienteering [1]. Choir activities are also available, and the federation notes that children develop social skills through these clubs [1].","synthesisMethod":"cursor"},{"area":"ethos","score":40,"confidence":0.4,"summary":"Strong publicly visible evidence for ethos and values (7 specific items). Themes include british values, character, community, ethos.","themes":["british values","character","community","ethos","moral","respect","safe","spiritual","values","vision","welcoming"],"offerings":[],"signals":[{"text":"The fundamental British Values of Democracy, Rule of Law, Mutual Respect, Tolerance and Individual Liberty are embedded within the vision, values, ethos and curriculum of the federation.","sourceUrl":"https://balksburyfederation.co.uk/vision-and-values/","sourceType":"school-website","capturedAt":"2026-08-06","pageTitle":"Vision and Values - Balksbury Federation Infant and Junior Schools","section":"ethos"},{"text":"Our Motto Learning and Growing Together British Values Balksbury Federation is committed to supporting our children as Balksbury Citizens so that they grow within their spiritual, moral, social and cultural development.","sourceUrl":"https://balksburyfederation.co.uk/vision-and-values/","sourceType":"school-website","capturedAt":"2026-08-06","pageTitle":"Vision and Values - Balksbury Federation Infant and Junior Schools","section":"ethos"}],"narrativeSummary":"Fundamental British Values of democracy, rule of law, mutual respect, tolerance and individual liberty are embedded within the federation\u2019s vision, values, ethos and curriculum [1]. Its culture promotes mutual respect and a sense of collaboration across protected characteristics, with equality seen as achievable only when the whole federated community works together [2]. The federation also aims to provide a safe, secure and welcoming learning environment, ensuring children gain a wealth of educational experiences from Year R to Year 6 [3].","synthesisMethod":"cursor"},{"area":"behaviour","score":42,"confidence":0.615,"summary":"Moderate publicly visible evidence for behaviour and pastoral care (2 specific items). Listed provision includes A Federated Smart School Council.","themes":["behaviour","positive"],"offerings":["A Federated Smart School Council"],"signals":[{"text":"Balksbury Wellbeing Team Statement: A Federated Smart School Council","sourceUrl":"https://balksburyfederation.co.uk/wellbeing/","sourceType":"school-website","capturedAt":"2026-08-06","pageTitle":"Wellbeing - Balksbury Federation Infant and Junior Schools","section":"behaviour"},{"text":"It is the intent of the federation that children begin their lifelong learning journey by developing physically, verbally, cognitively and emotionally whilst also embedding the federation\u2019s positive behaviour and attitudes to school and a love of learning.","sourceUrl":"https://balksburyfederation.co.uk/download/24/curriculum/466/balksbury-federation-curriculum-model.pdf","sourceType":"school-document","capturedAt":"2026-08-06","pageTitle":"balksbury federation curriculum model","section":"curriculum"}],"narrativeSummary":"Pastoral and wellbeing support includes a Federated Smart School Council, referenced in the Balksbury Wellbeing Team statement [1]. The federation intends that children begin their lifelong learning journey by developing physically, verbally, cognitively and emotionally, while embedding positive behaviour, attitudes to school and a love of learning [2].","synthesisMethod":"cursor"},{"area":"send","score":40,"confidence":0.4,"summary":"Strong publicly vi